{
 "_doc": [
  "Thresholds for `python -m oilpaint eval compare A B`.  A is the reference run (baseline), B the candidate.",
  "rules: first match wins; `match` is an fnmatch pattern on the flattened metric key, e.g. sheet.strata_sky.hairline, scenes.storm_v3@1600.regions.sky.bristle_L (a `*` also matches dots).",
  "direction: lower = smaller is better; higher = larger is better; match = any drift is bad; true = must be true in B; info = never reported.",
  "warn / fail: how much WORSE than A is tolerated, as {abs, rel}; the tolerance is max(abs, rel*|A|).  Worse than warn -> WARN, worse than fail -> FAIL, better by more than warn -> better.",
  "`eval compare` exits 1 if any FAIL (or any WARN with --strict), 2 if the runs have different widths (use --force to override).  Metrics with no matching rule are not compared.",
  "Copy this file, edit the numbers and pass --thresholds my.json.  Tolerances were set from run-to-run noise (same seed: 0) and from the size of the visible effect of the known flaws, see README 'Evaluating changes'."
 ],
 "rules": [
  {
   "match": "system.determinism.strokes_identical",
   "direction": "true",
   "why": "same seed must give bit-identical strokes"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.determinism.seed_changes_strokes",
   "direction": "true",
   "why": "a different seed must give different strokes"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.determinism.image_near_identical",
   "direction": "true",
   "why": "same strokes must replay to the same image"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.determinism.planner_identical",
   "direction": "true",
   "why": "a tiny planned scene must plan identically twice"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.determinism.replay_max_abs_diff_*",
   "direction": "lower",
   "fail": {
    "abs": 0.001,
    "rel": 0.0
   },
   "why": "replay of the same strokes twice"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.speed.strokes_per_s",
   "direction": "higher",
   "warn": {
    "abs": 0,
    "rel": 0.2
   },
   "fail": {
    "abs": 0,
    "rel": 0.5
   },
   "why": "explicit-stroke replay speed; noisy on a shared machine, re-run before believing a WARN"
  },
  {
   "match": "system.speed.light_seconds",
   "direction": "lower",
   "warn": {
    "abs": 0,
    "rel": 0.3
   },
   "fail": {
    "abs": 0,
    "rel": 0.8
   },
   "why": "relight time of the sheet"
  },
  {
